From 4799e3c67bd382c34b13d521b32ed164c72b6cc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): pipeline the sliced SP Engram row exchange under
 sparknet

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Immediate base: spark-ds41f-1107's vLLM series with candidate-49's 0762..0765
(624df94d82c2dccd246b3db7a7eb7ad00c04f64a in the prepared tree).

Rationale:
Under sparknet's one-shot RoCE policy, _tp_pynccl_comm() returned None, so
SPRows.project_exchange_rows always projected all T rows, ran then(), and only
then exchanged them (exchange_rows); its sliced pipeline never ran on any
served shape. Return the PyNCCL communicator beside the one-shot one
(_tp_roce_comm()) so a projection of two or more slices takes that pipeline:
each slice's peer blocks are projected into a send buffer and exchanged on the
side stream with copy_self=False while this rank's own block and the next
slice are projected. Engram projections run in two slices from 6,144 tokens
(ENGRAM_SLICE_TOKENS, was 2,048), where the per-slice GEMM is large enough
for the overlap to pay. One slice keeps 1107's path: one full-row projection,
then(), and the TP group's row exchange (one-shot RoCE when the rows fit,
else PyNCCL). SPRows.exchange_into now passes both send and recv to
should_exchange, since the one-shot exchange checks both before it runs.

Rework (candidate-49, round 1): the first version also sent gather_many
(gather_mxfp8) through the one-shot RoCE all-gather, packing the small
trailing tensors, and overlapped the one-slice exchange with then() on the
side stream. On sp1..sp4 (four GB10 ranks over 200G RoCE, the own-mark bench)
the one-shot gather was never faster than one grouped PyNCCL all-gather on
direct at the sizes it admits (own mark: +9% to +50% slowest-rank at
T=160..2048; this rework: +46% at T=2048, within the interval below), and on
ring4 it showed no consistent win (in this rework's session the first
version's boots read slower than 1107 beyond the interval at T=512 and 1024,
while a ring4-only variant running the same gather code read faster at
T=512). The one-slice overlap hides at most then() (one short elementwise
sum); no gain of it held across the two sessions, and in both it read slower
than 1107 beyond the interval at some T. Both are dropped: gather_many is
1107's grouped PyNCCL all-gather, and every T below 6,144 runs 1107's code.

Measured (slowest-rank median of 40 iterations, mean of two boots each, this
rework's same-session mirrored ABBA on sp1..sp4), project_exchange_rows of the
Engram wkv projection, without this patch -> with it:
- ring4 (tp4-ring): T=6144 11,950 -> 9,987 us (-16.4%), T=8192 15,527 ->
  12,691 us (-18.3%);
- direct (switched shapes): T=6144 10,982 -> 8,910 us (-18.9%), T=8192
  13,875 -> 11,889 us (-14.3%);
each beyond the two-boot interval, on rank 0 too. The first version measured
9,815 / 12,617 / 8,914 / 11,790 us in the same session. Below 6,144 tokens,
and in every gather_mxfp8 cell, this patch runs the same code as 1107.

Quality:
Bit-exact. Each rank's project_exchange_rows rows and then() output, and each
rank's gathered MXFP8 values, scales, top-k weights and ids, have the same
sha256 in every boot of every arm (corrected, without this patch, and the
first version) on ring4 and direct, and equal the in-process serial reference.

Tests:
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py
  tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py on GB10 (sp2, tests/conftest.py
  with the release-test tblib stub): 396 passed.
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py
  tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py with no visible device: 219 passed,
  17 skipped.
- test_project_exchange_rows_cuda_with_active_roce_comm and
  test_project_exchange_rows_roce_and_pynccl_coexistence check the one-slice
  order (projection, then(), row exchange) and the two-slice PyNCCL pipeline
  with an active one-shot communicator; test_gather_many_keeps_grouped_pynccl_beside_roce
  checks that gather_many stays on grouped PyNCCL.

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 sequence-parallel prefill optimization for
sparknet's one-shot RoCE policy; not applicable upstream.
